          explore multiple alternatives, or cumulatively to explore one
          alternative with multiple features.
          <br /><br />
          Nodes in current software are usually parametric containers for a
          “future” pipeline execution to get an output. But why can't we use
          node as a unit itself that each has an individual state so that it
          encodes information about “past” while still being able to progress to
          “future”? Each DesignTrace Node is a visual stateful unit that
          contains an interactive canvas with a local temporal history of image
          generation and editing actions. Users can do image editing just as in
          other non-AI creative software in each node, go back and forth within
          the node local editing history within one version; while dynamically
          applying semantics to branch out new nodes and using different nodes
          to explore, reuse and restart on different versions. Node collapse
          helps users tidy up their space quickly. The whole trace with visuals
          and arrows indicate the design progression on a larger and longer
